    "summary": "High‑energy MSG ’82 show with scorching Shakedown Street & monster Scarlet>Fire",
    "review": "The September 20, 1982 Madison Square Garden gig is a pure burst of Dead firepower. From the opening “Shakedown Street” – which often stretches into a twelve‑minute jam that Jerry slashes with razor‑sharp leads and Brent’s playful keyboards – through a blistering second set highlighted by the legendary Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain segue, the band is locked in. The setlist rolls smoothly into a monster Throwing Stones → Day Job pairing, a soaring Terrapin Station, and an epic Truckin’ → The Other One → Stella Blue → Sugar Magnolia closing that keeps the Garden buzzing. Brent Mydland’s keys are “right on target” all night, Phil’s bass anchors the improvisations (notably his four‑string intro to The Other One), and Bill/Kreutzmann provide a tight yet fluid rhythmic foundation. Though a few audience tapes note minor hiccups, the overall energy is sky‑high and the performance remains one of ’82’s most memorable MSG outings.",
